            "body_html": "<h2>Default Scenario</h2>\n<p>This section presents projected effects under our default tariff policy scenario. This scenario can\nbe thought of as a \"current law\" concept, where official policy, including changes officially\nscheduled to come into effect later this year, is taken as given. In addition to the tariffs\ncurrently in place as of late August 2026 (including the Section 338 tariffs on Canadian products that\ntook effect on August 22), this scenario includes scheduled tariff increases in October\n(pharmaceutical tariffs under Section 232) and December (polysilicon tariffs under Section 232.)</p>\n<p>This is not a forecast of where tariff policy will end up, but rather a useful scorekeeping\nbenchmark. Alternative policy scenarios are explored in the next tab.</p>\n<p>Estimated impacts are measured against a January 2025 tariff-policy baseline. That is, these\nnumbers answer the question: going forward, what will the impacts of tariffs be <em>relative to a\nworld where the Trump administration never changed tariff policy</em>?</p>",
            "section": "overview",
