            "body_html": "<h2>Alternative Scenarios</h2>\n<p>These figures show the same projected effects as the Default Scenario tab, but across both current\nlaw and several modeled policy scenarios. Use the <strong>View</strong> toggle to switch between each scenario's\nown effects (levels) and its effect relative to our default scenario (change vs. default).</p>\n<p>We include three alternative scenarios in this release:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Excluding the Section 338 tariffs.</strong> This scenario is identical to current law except that it\n  omits the Section 338 tariff actions on Canadian products, which took effect on August 22.</li>\n<li><strong>Excluding the Section 301 tariff actions taken since January 2025.</strong> This scenario is\n  identical to current law except that it omits the Section 301 tariff actions on Brazil and the\n  forced-labor tariffs. It keeps in place the Section 301 tariffs on China imposed before 2025.</li>\n<li><strong>Excluding the Section 232 tariffs.</strong> This scenario is identical to current law except that it\n  omits all Section 232 tariffs on steel, aluminum, and other products.</li>\n</ul>",
            "section": "overview",
